<task id="060" project="email-communication-solution-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Migrate SummarizeFilesDialog, FilePreviewDialog, DocumentEmailWizard to the canonical `&lt;EmailComposer /&gt;`</title>
    <phase>Wave 6 — Client caller migration + retirements</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>7</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>021, 022, 043</dependencies>
    <blocks>062</blocks>
    <tags>frontend, refactoring, communication</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Removes an inline `fetch` to `/api/communications/send` from a production-shipped shared-lib component (SummarizeFilesDialog ~line 436), migrates a LegalWorkspace dialog fork (FilePreviewDialog), and fixes a latent attachment-ID payload bug (DocumentEmailWizard ~line 494). Modifies `.tsx` in `@spaarke/ui-components` consumed by multiple solutions; must respect ADR-045 (canonical send), ADR-019 (typed error), ADR-021 (Fluent v9), ADR-028 (no direct `@spaarke/auth` import in shared lib).</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W6</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches only the three dialog files (SummarizeFilesDialog, FilePreviewDialog, DocumentEmailWizard) — disjoint from task 061 (wizards + CreateMatter fork). Both may run concurrently after W2 wrappers (021/022) and W4 Code Page (043) land.</parallel-reason>
    <fr-refs>FR-21</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Migrate three ad-hoc/inline email-send surfaces to the canonical `&lt;EmailComposer /&gt;` engine (via its `SendEmailStep`/`SendEmailDialog` wrappers from W2 task 021) and the typed `sendCommunication()` wrapper (W2 task 022):

    1. **SummarizeFilesDialog** — `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SummarizeFilesWizard/SummarizeFilesDialog.tsx`. Remove the inline `fetch` to `/api/communications/send` at ~line 436 (empirically confirmed per R4 CLAUDE.md finding #6 / R3 pre-flight). Replace with the canonical inline-mount `&lt;SendEmailStep /&gt;`; the wizard's Finish action invokes `composerRef.current.send()`. Preserve ALL non-send behavior (file selection, summary generation, wizard navigation).

    2. **FilePreviewDialog** — the LegalWorkspace dialog that sends email from the preview surface. Migrate to the canonical `&lt;SendEmailDialog /&gt;` wrapper; move legacy success/error side effects into `onSent`/`onError` handlers that consume the typed `SendCommunicationError`.

    3. **DocumentEmailWizard** — `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DocumentEmailWizard/DocumentEmailWizard.tsx`. Fix the latent attachment-ID bug at ~line 494 (empirically confirmed): it currently maps `d.documentId` (`sprk_document` GUIDs) into the attachment field, causing attachments to silently fail. Send the canonical **`attachmentDriveItemIds`** sourced from `wizardContext.uploadedFiles[].driveItemId` (SPE driveItem IDs). Remove `attachmentDocumentIds` from this caller entirely.

    After this task, none of the three files call `fetch` to `/api/communications/send` and DocumentEmailWizard ships the correct driveItem IDs. Smoke tests run in task 062's flow / W4 UI tests.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke frontend engineer authoritative on `@spaarke/ui-components` dialog/wizard surfaces, the canonical `&lt;EmailComposer /&gt;` wrapper API (W2 task 021), the typed `sendCommunication()` + `SendCommunicationError` contract (W2 task 022), and the attachment-ID confusion failure mode (FAILURE-MODES AP-4).
  </role>

  <goal>
    All three dialogs consume the canonical composer: `SummarizeFilesDialog` and `FilePreviewDialog` have zero `fetch.*communications/send` references and route sends through the wrapper's internal `sendCommunication()`; `DocumentEmailWizard` sends `attachmentDriveItemIds` from `driveItemId` (grep for `attachmentDocumentIds` in that file returns zero). `@spaarke/ui-components` `npm run build:prod` + `npm run lint` are clean; no shared-lib component imports `@spaarke/auth` directly (`authenticatedFetch` flows via props).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      This is the R4 consolidation of R3's Wave 3/4/5 caller-migration tasks (R3 tasks 051, 060, 075) into a single dialog-migration task. The canonical engine + wrappers now exist (W2), and the Communication Code Page is deployed (W4), so these ad-hoc send paths can be retired. SummarizeFilesDialog's inline `fetch` and DocumentEmailWizard's `documentId`-vs-`driveItemId` bug are the two highest-leverage latent defects this closes. FilePreviewDialog is a LegalWorkspace fork that must route through the shared canonical wrapper (no LegalWorkspace email-component forks per ADR-045).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SummarizeFilesWizard/SummarizeFilesDialog.tsx (PRIMARY — inline fetch ~line 436)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/DocumentEmailWizard/DocumentEmailWizard.tsx (PRIMARY — attachment-ID bug ~line 494)</file>
      <file>src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/components/**/FilePreviewDialog.tsx (LegalWorkspace preview-send dialog)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/wrappers/SendEmailStep.tsx (canonical inline wrapper — W2 task 021)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/wrappers/SendEmailDialog.tsx (canonical dialog wrapper — W2 task 021)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/communicationApi.ts (`sendCommunication()` + `SendCommunicationError` + `attachmentDriveItemIds` — W2 task 022)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">MUST NOT call `fetch` to `/api/communications/send` directly. All UX sends go through a canonical wrapper; programmatic sends through `sendCommunication()`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Error paths consume the typed `SendCommunicationError` parsed from ProblemDetails.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Composer chrome is Fluent UI v9; inherited via the canonical wrapper.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Shared-lib components MUST NOT import `@spaarke/auth` directly; `authenticatedFetch` is injected via props.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec FR-13/FR-21">DocumentEmailWizard uses canonical `attachmentDriveItemIds` (SPE driveItem IDs), never `sprk_document` GUIDs; `attachmentDocumentIds` removed from the caller.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Preserve all non-send behavior in each dialog (summary generation, preview rendering, file selection, wizard navigation).</constraint>
    <constraint source="repo">`npm run build:prod` + `npm run lint` in `@spaarke/ui-components` remain green (use `build:prod`, not `build`, per root CLAUDE.md §12).</constraint>
  </constraints>

